course: dictionary
lesson: 5157
title: Irregular: not the usual pattern
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Irregular means not following the usual pattern. Something is irregular when it is not even, or when it does not happen at equal times. «The coastline was irregular, with bays and jagged rocks.» The coast is not a neat, smooth line, so irregular means not even in shape.
explain: Irregular also describes timing. «The bus came at irregular times, so we never knew when to wait.» There was no steady pattern, so you could not predict it. Ask yourself: is there a regular pattern here, or does it jump about?
explain: In grammar, irregular words break the normal rule. Most verbs add -ed to make the past, like jump and jumped. But go becomes went, and swim becomes swam. You cannot work these out by a rule, so you learn them by heart.
fact: Irregular means not following the usual pattern, rule or shape.
fact: «An irregular shape» has sides or angles that are not all equal.
fact: «Irregular verbs» do not add -ed: swim, swam; run, ran; go, went; catch, caught.
fact: Irregular verbs come in little families: sing, sang, sung; ring, rang, rung; think, thought; buy, bought.
fact: Good, better, best and bad, worse, worst are irregular comparisons.
exercise: «The coastline was irregular, with bays and jagged rocks.» What does irregular mean here? | Perfectly straight and smooth | Very cold and icy | *Not even or smooth in shape | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The bus came at irregular times.» What does irregular mean here? | Very fast | Always at exactly ten o'clock | *Not at equal, steady times | Free of charge
exercise: Which verb is irregular, so its past does not add -ed? | play | talk | jump | *swim
test: Which is the past form of run? | *ran | running | runned | runs
test: Which word means not the same shape all over? | Regular | *Irregular | Round | Even
exam: Which sentence uses irregular in the grammar sense? | The sun is hot today. | *Irregular verbs like catch and caught must be learned by heart. | Turn left at the old sign. | The cat sat on the mat.
